#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:160002
#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:290002
#: 812c6da9be384e87b831944a0dd57097 981e0a407fb542ad9c0c502a0930a62a
msgid "Parametrizing by Half-Life"
msgstr "Parametrización por vida media"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:160004
#: 13fe655134f44f6ab7a90cd5c7cbc1c5
msgid ""
"$\\alpha$ is a retention rate: the share of the effect that survives one "
"period. That is convenient mathematically, but awkward to discuss with "
"stakeholders, who rarely have an intuition for what $\\alpha = 0.7$ buys "
"them. The **half-life** — the number of periods until the effect has "
"decayed by half — is easier to reason about."
msgstr ""
"$\\alpha$ es una tasa de retención: la proporción del efecto que sobrevive "
"un período. Eso es conveniente matemáticamente, pero resulta incómodo de "
"discutir con las partes interesadas, que rara vez tienen una intuición de lo"
" que les aporta un $\\alpha = 0.7$. La **vida media** — el número de "
"períodos hasta que el efecto ha decaído a la mitad — es más fácil de "
"razonar."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:160006
#: a8c39d6fe30942caaf93a17cce446d35
msgid ""
"The two are one-to-one. Since the weight at lag $t$ is $\\alpha^t$, a "
"half-life $h$ corresponds to"
msgstr ""
"Ambas se corresponden una a una. Dado que el peso en el rezago $t$ es "
"$\\alpha^t$, una vida media $h$ corresponde a"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:160008
#: fce40a4327ca4fa5a34b78939e2c5598
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\alpha = 0.5^{1 / h}"
msgstr "\\alpha = 0.5^{1 / h}"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:160010
#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:290018
#: 02e168c65a374f10be5085cfc4a810ce e1d57ed7f71a4e98bfc37672397436a4
msgid ""
"Any positive half-life maps into $(0, 1)$, so the constraint on $\\alpha$"
" is satisfied automatically. Pass `parametrization=\"halflife\"` to put a"
" prior on the half-life instead:"
msgstr ""
"Cualquier vida media positiva se transforma en un valor dentro de $(0, 1)$, "
"por lo que la restricción sobre $\\alpha$ se satisface automáticamente. Pase"
" `parametrization=\"halflife\"` para colocar un prior sobre la vida media en"
" su lugar:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:160019
#: 0defd73672f041d6b1457acbad7f92b7
msgid ""
"The sampled variable is then `adstock_halflife` rather than "
"`adstock_alpha`."
msgstr ""
"La variable muestreada es entonces `adstock_halflife` en lugar de "
"`adstock_alpha`."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:160021
#: 37522f35024e4c23880e24c1eb5856b7
msgid ""
"The half-life means exactly what it says for any `l_max` and for either "
"setting of `normalize`. Truncating the kernel drops later lags without "
"touching earlier ones, and normalizing divides every weight by the same "
"constant, so the ratio $w_h / w_0 = 0.5$ survives both. Each curve below "
"crosses the dashed line at its own half-life."
msgstr ""
"La vida media significa exactamente lo que dice para cualquier `l_max` y "
"para cualquier valor de `normalize`. Truncar el kernel elimina los rezagos "
"posteriores sin afectar a los anteriores, y normalizar divide todos los "
"pesos por la misma constante, de modo que la razón $w_h / w_0 = 0.5$ se "
"conserva en ambos casos. Cada curva de abajo cruza la línea discontinua en "
"su propia vida media."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:180002
#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:310002
#: e8b0c1b1cff64a1195f06ea5617fa7fc ecf472ccf4f0484f96dc06c7cdad6ca7
msgid "Choosing a Prior on the Half-Life"
msgstr "Elegir un prior para la vida media"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:180004
#: ed33caa7dc484e8c9c0eb86187c6a188
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The default is `InverseGamma(2.6, 1)`, picked so that switching "
"parametrization is a change of coordinates rather than a change of model."
" Pushed through $\\alpha = 0.5^{1/h}$ it implies a median $\\alpha$ of "
"0.207, against 0.206 for the default `Beta(1, 3)`. The tails are close "
"too: the 5th and 95th percentiles of $\\alpha$ are 0.019 and 0.651, "
"against 0.017 and 0.632 under `Beta(1, 3)`."
msgstr ""
"El valor predeterminado es `InverseGamma(2.6, 1)`, elegido para que cambiar "
"de parametrización sea un cambio de coordenadas y no un cambio de modelo. Al"
" transformarlo mediante $\\alpha = 0.5^{1/h}$, implica una mediana de "
"$\\alpha$ de 0.207, frente a 0.206 del `Beta(1, 3)` predeterminado. Las "
"colas también son cercanas: los percentiles 5 y 95 de $\\alpha$ son 0.019 y "
"0.651, frente a 0.017 y 0.632 con `Beta(1, 3)`."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:180006
#: c3b8fd5bef374b7a8883ffcf39f44c97
msgid ""
"Read as a half-life, the default is short: a median of 0.44 periods. A "
"channel you expect to carry over for weeks needs a prior of its own."
msgstr ""
"Interpretado como una vida media, el valor predeterminado es corto: una "
"mediana de 0.44 períodos. Un canal cuyo efecto de arrastre se espera que "
"dure semanas necesita un prior propio."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:180008
#: c6463afce43c48b5b22347a430ea7e21
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"If you supply your own prior, keep its mass away from zero. The gradient "
"$d\\alpha / dh = \\alpha \\ln(2) / h^2$ underflows to exactly zero for "
"$h$ below roughly $10^{-3}$, which leaves the likelihood numerically flat"
" there and gives the sampler nothing to climb. That rules out "
"`HalfNormal`, `Exponential` and `Gamma` with a shape below one, natural "
"as those are for a positive parameter."
msgstr ""
"Si proporciona su propio prior, mantenga su masa alejada de cero. El "
"gradiente $d\\alpha / dh = \\alpha \\ln(2) / h^2$ se hace exactamente cero "
"por underflow para $h$ por debajo de aproximadamente $10^{-3}$, lo que deja "
"la verosimilitud numéricamente plana en esa zona y no le da al muestreador "
"nada por donde subir. Eso descarta `HalfNormal`, `Exponential` y `Gamma` con"
" un parámetro de forma menor que uno, por naturales que resulten para un "
"parámetro positivo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:190002
#: 71ae7ef5d2f749aa9175220923369cb5
msgid "Apply Geometric Adstock to Channel Data"
msgstr "Aplicar el adstock geométrico a los datos de los canales"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:200002
#: 34bf2fba0e6942f4b59bc88b70174666
msgid ""
"Now that we understand how geometric adstock decay curves work in theory,"
" let's see what happens when we apply this transformation to **real "
"marketing spend data**."
msgstr ""
"Ahora que entendemos cómo funcionan en teoría las curvas de decaimiento del "
"adstock geométrico, veamos qué ocurre cuando aplicamos esta transformación a"
" **datos reales de gasto de marketing**."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:200004
#: cde8571921f04ffd89e8d49ed7b01256
msgid "What We're Doing"
msgstr "Qué estamos haciendo"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:200006
#: bb77e82a79724cc8a25a2533e6b5f432
#, python-format
msgid ""
"We'll take the raw weekly spend from our two marketing channels (`x1` and"
" `x2`) and transform them using geometric adstock with **α = 0.5** "
"(moderate decay). This represents a realistic scenario where advertising "
"effects carry over for several weeks, roughly 50% of the impact remains "
"after one week, 25% after two weeks, and so on."
msgstr ""
"Tomaremos el gasto semanal sin procesar de nuestros dos canales de marketing"
" (`x1` y `x2`) y lo transformaremos con adstock geométrico con **α = 0.5** "
"(decaimiento moderado). Esto representa un escenario realista en el que los "
"efectos publicitarios se arrastran durante varias semanas: aproximadamente "
"el 50% del impacto permanece después de una semana, el 25% después de dos "
"semanas, y así sucesivamente."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:200008
#: 3bc8f4bb777147d894ef6ff41b3bd20b
msgid "Why This Matters"
msgstr "Por qué esto es importante"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:200010
#: 24c2b77d62fe47968c303522779449de
msgid ""
"Remember, in the raw data, a spike in spend only appears in that single "
"week. But in reality, that advertising doesn't just create impact on the "
"day it runs. It creates **memories** in consumers' minds that influence "
"their behavior for weeks afterward. The adstock transformation adjusts "
"our spend data to reflect this cumulative, lingering effect."
msgstr ""
"Recuerde que, en los datos sin procesar, un pico de gasto aparece únicamente"
" en esa semana. Pero en la realidad, esa publicidad no solo genera impacto "
"el día en que se emite. Crea **recuerdos** en la mente de los consumidores "
"que influyen en su comportamiento durante las semanas posteriores. La "
"transformación de adstock ajusta nuestros datos de gasto para reflejar este "
"efecto acumulativo y persistente."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:200012
#: 8e416e1d81c748a485355a3aece7620b
msgid "What to Look For"
msgstr "Qué observar"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:200014
#: 3fec837194584d02a9e730be02559d86
msgid "When we compare the original spend to the adstocked spend, you'll notice:"
msgstr ""
"Cuando comparamos el gasto original con el gasto con adstock, notaremos lo "
"siguiente:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:200016
#: c4af4053c23d43008d92e2e9c25870d6
msgid ""
"**Smoothing**: The adstocked curves are smoother than the raw spend "
"because each week's value incorporates carryover from previous weeks"
msgstr ""
"**Suavizado**: Las curvas con adstock son más suaves que el gasto sin "
"procesar porque el valor de cada semana incorpora el efecto de arrastre de "
"las semanas anteriores"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:200017
#: 8d49b37f1766495b9c3e5c27211cc3f2
msgid ""
"**Elevated Baselines**: After periods of high spend, the adstocked values"
" remain elevated even when spend drops to zero—this is the \"memory "
"effect\""
msgstr ""
"**Líneas base elevadas**: Tras períodos de gasto alto, los valores con "
"adstock se mantienen elevados incluso cuando el gasto baja a cero; este es "
"el \"efecto de memoria\""

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:200018
#: 334fc6b335224fdd8aba66d812ff7fb5
msgid ""
"**Delayed Peaks**: The peak adstocked values may occur slightly after the"
" peak raw spend, as the full effect accumulates over time"
msgstr ""
"**Picos retardados**: Los picos de los valores con adstock pueden ocurrir "
"ligeramente después del pico del gasto sin procesar, ya que el efecto "
"completo se acumula con el tiempo"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:200019
#: dd45448d69234a2ebdceb5f3306a63e3
msgid ""
"**Realistic Impact**: The adstocked spend represents what the *effective "
"advertising pressure* looks like from a consumer's perspective"
msgstr ""
"**Impacto realista**: El gasto con adstock representa cómo se ve la *presión"
" publicitaria efectiva* desde la perspectiva del consumidor"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:200021
#: bc3a77215f85438a922eab2ee365aa0e
msgid ""
"This transformation is what we'll actually feed into our MMM model. "
"Instead of assuming that $100 spent in week 5 only affects sales in week "
"5, we're acknowledging that it affects sales in weeks 5, 6, 7... with "
"diminishing impact."
msgstr ""
"Esta transformación es lo que realmente introduciremos en nuestro modelo "
"MMM. En lugar de asumir que los $100 gastados en la semana 5 solo afectan "
"las ventas de la semana 5, reconocemos que afectan las ventas de las semanas"
" 5, 6, 7... con un impacto decreciente."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:210003
#: 8d95b25d02154fc2873d25f575e5506b
msgid ""
"We will follow this process for each type of Adstock transformation "
"throughout the notebook. The process will include exploring the different"
" curve behaviors as well as transforming our media spend with those "
"behaviors."
msgstr ""
"Seguiremos este proceso con cada tipo de transformación de adstock a lo "
"largo del cuaderno. El proceso incluirá explorar los distintos "
"comportamientos de las curvas, así como transformar nuestro gasto en medios "
"con esos comportamientos."

