msgid "3. Weibull CDF Adstock"
msgstr "3. Adstock Weibull CDF"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:350007
#: 47532276c17a4ad4a3ede5efbfbe897d
msgid ""
"Weibull CDF adstock uses the **cumulative distribution function**, "
"creating an **S-shaped curve** where effects build up gradually."
msgstr ""
"El adstock Weibull CDF utiliza la **función de distribución acumulada**, que"
" crea una **curva en forma de S** en la que los efectos se acumulan "
"gradualmente."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:350011
#: 3efe3e22b5e34f95899d60dbeeadf037
msgid ""
"The Weibull CDF is a function depending on two variables, $k$ (known as "
"the **shape**) and $\\lambda$ (known as the **scale**).   The idea is "
"closely related to geometric adstock but with one important difference : "
"the rate of decay (what we called $\\alpha$ in the geometric adstock "
"equation) is no longer fixed. Instead it's **time-dependent**."
msgstr ""
"La Weibull CDF es una función que depende de dos variables, $k$ (conocida "
"como la **forma**) y $\\lambda$ (conocida como la **escala**).   La idea "
"está estrechamente relacionada con el adstock geométrico, pero con una "
"diferencia importante : la tasa de decaimiento (lo que llamamos $\\alpha$ en"
" la ecuación del adstock geométrico) ya no es fija. En cambio, **depende del"
" tiempo**."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:350014
#: 04ba5d7bab694fa8a7e765e227c8256f
msgid "**The Weibull CDF adstock function therefore takes the form :**"
msgstr "**Por lo tanto, la función de adstock Weibull CDF tiene la forma :**"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:350016
#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:430017
#: 0bcacf41a2434066a1b382b1112f538b 59c65d827bd94bf4a1264e1ce6e6905c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\tilde{x}_t = x_t + \\alpha_t \\tilde{x}_{t-1}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\tilde{x}_t = x_t + \\alpha_t \\tilde{x}_{t-1}\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:350020
#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:430021
#: 7767fdc13de541bc8ddeb556be61fcf2 f22cd353cb9c4987acbf52f4207444bd
msgid "where $\\alpha_t$ is now a function of time $t$"
msgstr "donde $\\alpha_t$ es ahora una función del tiempo $t$"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:350022
#: c5db39fbcf914e09864ab8a947701bc7
msgid ""
"**The Weibull CDF is actually used to build the $\\alpha_t$'s, and it "
"takes the form :**"
msgstr ""
"**En realidad, la Weibull CDF se usa para construir los $\\alpha_t$, y tiene"
" la forma :**"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:350024
#: 5fd0b584f9c84b3fa22bb54ce412a920
msgid ""
"\n"
"F_{k, \\lambda}(t) = 1 - e^{-(\\frac{t}{\\lambda})^k}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"F_{k, \\lambda}(t) = 1 - e^{-(\\frac{t}{\\lambda})^k}\n"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:350028
#: 7222d363af2e4667814b1b334d5cf399
msgid "Then, $\\alpha_t$ is computed as :"
msgstr "Entonces, $\\alpha_t$ se calcula como :"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:350030
#: a5efd1ddf0fa4365a22142c773c22984
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\alpha_t = 1 - F_{k,\\lambda}(t)\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\alpha_t = 1 - F_{k,\\lambda}(t)\n"

