msgid "5. Binomial Adstock"
msgstr "5. Adstock binomial"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:510007
#: 6921c27428624515ac76c9903f15524a
msgid ""
"Binomial adstock provides a **flexible decay curve** based on the "
"binomial distribution."
msgstr ""
"El adstock binomial proporciona una **curva de decaimiento flexible** basada"
" en la distribución binomial."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:510011
#: 097db57dd6a44fb09a39ee314f007d53
msgid ""
"Binomial adstock assumes that the effect of one unit of spend at time $t$"
" is given by:"
msgstr ""
"El adstock binomial supone que el efecto de una unidad de gasto en el tiempo"
" $t$ está dado por:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:510013
#: 871b4f8d58ff42858a18bbd8247a0ef9
msgid ""
"f(t) = \\left(1 - \\frac{t}{L + 1} \\right)^{\\left(\\frac{1}{\\alpha} - "
"1\\right)}"
msgstr "f(t) = \\left(1 - \\frac{t}{L + 1} \\right)^{\\left(\\frac{1}{\\alpha} - 1\\right)}"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:510016
#: 07faea5efa22448aa4130cd818b3bae1
msgid "$t$ is the time since the advertising spend ($0 \\le t \\le L + 1$)"
msgstr ""
"$t$ es el tiempo transcurrido desde el gasto publicitario ($0 \\le t \\le L "
"+ 1$)"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:510017
#: f2b1810b4a394245b89a16c85868827d
msgid "$L$ is `l_max`, the maximum duration of carryover effect"
msgstr "$L$ es `l_max`, la duración máxima del efecto de arrastre"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:510018
#: 279154aba2bd4539b9ee3a1ca2e4247c
msgid "$\\alpha \\in (0, 1)$ is the shape parameter controlling the decay curve"
msgstr ""
"$\\alpha \\in (0, 1)$ es el parámetro de forma que controla la curva de "
"decaimiento"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:510019
#: 8ec2f64ef1fb407e84b9bdec1b7842d4
msgid "Notice that $f(L + 1) = 0$"
msgstr "Observe que $f(L + 1) = 0$"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:510021
#: 7b6e78da32444fb2807ec02fe0afaa95
msgid ""
"The binomial adstock transformation provides more flexible decay shapes "
"compared to geometric adstock. The $\\alpha$ parameter controls both the "
"shape and the decay rate, allowing for convex and concave decay patterns."
msgstr ""
"La transformación de adstock binomial ofrece formas de decaimiento más "
"flexibles que el adstock geométrico. El parámetro $\\alpha$ controla tanto "
"la forma como la tasa de decaimiento, lo que permite patrones de decaimiento"
" convexos y cóncavos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/adstock_functions_guide.ipynb:510024
#: 6af6179b8151459eb0c38271b2b50237
msgid "When you need **more flexible decay shapes** than geometric"
msgstr ""
"Cuando se necesitan **formas de decaimiento más flexibles** que la "
"geométrica"

